to run:

- have homebrew and clang installed
- run "brew install websocketpp"
- run "g++ -std=c++17 -I/opt/homebrew/opt/websocketpp/include \
    -I/opt/homebrew/opt/boost/include -I/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/include \
    -I/opt/homebrew/opt/jsoncpp/include -L/opt/homebrew/opt/boost/lib \
    -L/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib -L/opt/homebrew/opt/jsoncpp/lib \
    -o eth_mempool_monitor eth_mempool_monitor.cpp -lboost_system -lssl -lcrypto -ljsoncpp -lcurl
" or something similar (depending on where your dependencies are installed)

-run  ./eth_mempool_monitor <HTTPS QUICKNOE ENDPOINT>

you should see pending ethereum transactions print out 



ON LINUX 


sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install libssl-dev
sudo apt-get install libjsoncpp-devy
sudo apt-get install libcurl4-openssl-dev
sudo apt-get install libwebsocketpp-dev

g++ -std=c++17 -o pending_tx full_node_monitor_mempool.cpp -lboost_system -lpthread -lcurl -ljsoncpp -lssl -lcrypto


for sending eth:

run this in geth ge:

> personal.importRawKey("YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY", "YOUR_PASSWORD")
"0xYourAccountAddress"

personal.unlockAccount("0xYourAccountAddress", "YOUR_PASSWORD", 3600) // Unlock for 1 hour
